sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-thompson1917-t1917-029> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Thompson (1917) T1917-029: logarithmic-spiral chamber succession with constant ratio vs Shi (2021) fusulinid half-whorl series faithfully reproduces Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model morphology" ;
        dct:description "The simulation script(s) thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py, docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json, datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib, morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
        dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean>,
            <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean; output: docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_comparison.png; organism: Fusulinida (Triticites, Pseudoschwagerina, Sphaeroschwagerina, Zellia, Robustoschwagerina); Thompson's figured genera via the generative model; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1, lean 4.35.0, lockfile requirements.lock.txt (NOT the versions used here — pip resolved newer numpy/matplotlib/Pillow); claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Thompson (1917) pp. 591-598: chambers/whorls in continued proportion lie on a logarithmic spiral; von Moller's Fusulina whorls in ratio ~1.5 (half-whorl 1.225, alpha ~86 deg); van Iterson's Triloculina 1.323; Rhumbler's Pulvinulina ~1.187 with a 'small secondary fluctuation'; constant volume ratio from growth proportional to existing mass. | Thompson (1917) pp. 602-605: rotaline, Miliolid, Nodosarian, Textularian, Orbitolitid forms are all logarithmic-spiral cases differing in numerical coefficients and pass into one another by continuous gradations.; reconstructed_in_script: A discrete similar-chamber generative model (centres on r = r0 rho^k at angle k d, radii a0 rho^k, optional translation) that Thompson describes verbally; chamber size a0 and overlap are free choices, not source parameters. | Per-specimen log-linear fits of test DIAMETER (perpendicular to the coiling axis, PCA frame from the mid-ontogeny outline) vs half-whorl stage on the Dryad outlines; BIC comparison with linear growth; CV and linear trend of successive ratios; a gap/overlap statistic for genus continuity; pre-registered pass/fail thresholds (r >= 0.98, 80 %, CV <= 0.15, +/-0.05, gap ratio <= 6). | Longest-segment rule for the 14 specimens digitised at two magnifications.; transfer_boundary: Dryad outlines are whorl-level axial sections in pixels of Late Paleozoic fusulinids; Thompson's chamber-level claims (septal chambers, Miliolidae, rotaline forms) are tested only via his own printed tables and the generative model, not via new specimen measurements. | The fusulinid thin-section photograph is displayed but not measured in v1.; does_not_claim: Does not claim that the growth ratio is physiologically caused by mass-proportional growth (E4 is proved algebraically, not tested). | Does not claim the verdict generalises to planktonic or miliolid foraminifera; n = 5 fusulinid genera, 106 specimens, one Dryad deposit. | The T4 'continuity' statistic is a heuristic with an arbitrary threshold; its FAIL in v1 (gap ratio 6.34 vs 6.0) is not evidence of discontinuity.]; other sources: On Growth and Form — Ch. XII The Spiral Shells of the Foraminifera (pp. 587-611, Figs. 308-317) <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom>, Die spiral-gewundenen Foraminiferen des russischen Kohlenkalks <https://archive.org/details/ongrowthform1917thom/page/n612>, Geometric analysis of shell coiling: general problems <https://www.jstor.org/stable/1301992>, File:Fusulinid.jpg — fusulinid axial thin section (CC BY-SA 2.5, ja:User:NEON) <https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fusulinid.jpg>" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1017/pab.2020.53>,
            <https://doi.org/10.5061/dryad.sn02v6x26> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/paper_citations.bib" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/result.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_metrics.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "datasets/thompson_1917/t1917-029/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_reference.json" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "docs/media/t1917_029_the_spiral_shells_of_the_foram_growth.gif" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "morphoeval/lean/loops/Thompson1917_T1917_029.lean" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" .
    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "thompson/claims/t1917-029_the-spiral-shells-of-the-foraminifera.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" .
}

